# UST.G3BS H02 Endpoint Action at Root Five Theorem v1

## Result

At the G3BR proof place `(p,gamma)=(21817,5)`, evaluate every exact G3BK H11-to-H02 correction source

```text
R_P = -4 P s C
```

for all 1,013 frozen H11 residue monomials `P`, and solve them against the selected G3BI endpoint H02 chart.

The exact source matrix has shape `42706 x 1013` and 19,247 nonzero entries. The complete inverse action has 25,446,335 nonzero coordinates and zero residual. It retains

```text
251,207       H02 quotient coordinates
25,195,128    original-Jacobian preimage coordinates.
```

The canonical characteristic-zero source digest agrees exactly with G3BK. Thus G3BS is an evaluation of the already selected source, not a replacement or fitted proxy.

## Significance

G3BS closes the first production-size H02 action evaluation at one split root. Together with G3BR, it shows that the selected endpoint chart is not only known to exist but can execute all 1,013 required source columns exactly at the proof embedding.

## Exact scope

One root does not determine a degree-six number-field element. G3BS therefore does not claim six-root interpolation, a residue in the power basis, characteristic-zero reconstruction, recursive return of these preimages, integral G3BJ transport, or terminal physical readout.

